# Edenida rules

- This is a production SaaS, not a demo. Prefer maintainable, tested, secure code.
- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/STATUS.md` before substantial work.
- Stack: Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript strict, pnpm, Tailwind, shadcn, Supabase, Zod, Playwright.
- Never put Supabase service_role or secrets in client bundles.
- RLS required on exposed tables; guest PII must not appear in public website data.
- Website builder is block-based; keep content separate from presentation.
- Write Playwright coverage with features; use getByRole/getByLabel preferentially.
- Do not invent completion percentages; update `docs/STATUS.md` measurably.
- Conventional Commits; branch pattern `agent/<id>/<task>-<slug>` for agent work.
- Avoid drive-by refactors and unsolicited markdown files outside the docs plan.
